; The Expo SDK 54 / React Native 0.81 peer-dependency graph is not fully
; consistent under npm's strict peer resolution: @clerk/expo 3.2.x pulls
; @clerk/react 6.x and @clerk/shared 4.x, which peer react and react-dom
; "~19.1.4", while SDK 54 pins react 19.1.0 exactly (React Native 0.81.5's
; renderer is 19.1.0 and refuses any other react at runtime). npm itself
; resolves this with --legacy-peer-deps.
; package-lock.json IS committed (generated with this flag under Node 22) and
; CI installs with `npm ci`, which must resolve the tree the same way — so the
; flag stays for every install, local and CI.
legacy-peer-deps=true
